On Oct 2, 2009, at 10:10 , Markus Loecher wrote:

> Dear iplots developers,
> are there any plans (or existing functions that I have missed) to  
> have an interactive image plotting function in iplots or MONDRIAN,  
> sth. like the "i" version of image().
>

image() in R is nothing else but a grid passed to imap().


> I am asking partially because I would very much like to create some  
> useful links to the iplot package in my RgoogleMaps (http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/RgoogleMaps/index.html 
> ) package. I would use imap() but to plot the map background tile, I  
> first need to call image().

R has no support for true raster images, image() simply plots  
rectangles for each pixel - you can do that same e.g. with ilines().  
However, I do agree that it would be nice to have "true" support for  
raster images and it is planned for iPlots eXtreme.

Cheers,
Simon

